<title>USA: Unimed gets nod to sell drug in S. Africa.</title>
<headline>Unimed gets nod to sell drug in S. Africa.</headline>
<dateline>BUFFALO GROVE, Ill. 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unimed Pharmaceuticals Inc said Wednesday that its drug, Marinol, received regulatory approval in South Africa.</p>
<p>Marinol, approved as an appetite stimulant for AIDS patients and to reduce chemotherapy-related nausea, is being marketed in South Africa by Pharmacare Ltd. It is being sold under the trademark Elevat.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
